  "provenance": "Archives fetched over HTTPS from https://jeodpp.jrc.ec.europa.eu/ftp/jrc-opendata/EDGAR/datasets/v81_FT2022_AP_new/<SPECIES>/TOTALS/flx_nc/ (bc, oc, so2 on 2026-09-30; co, nox, nh3, nmvoc, pm25, pm10 on 2026-11-12 UTC, pollutant directories CO, NOx, NH3, NMVOC, PM2.5, PM10 as the server spells them), each selector's url, sha256 and size pinned above; each zip holds one NetCDF4 file with float32 fluxes(lat=1800, lon=3600) in kg m-2 s-1 on 0.1 deg cell centres (-89.95..89.95 N, -179.95..179.95 E) and a _readme.html. Annual 2022 totals, no seasonal, weekly or diurnal profile (a declared v1 simplification; the monthly sector files under .../monthly/ are the v2 route). remap bilinear on the flux density (woof.chem_inventory_frames, periodic in longitude) is not mass-exact; the conservative route is cell_sum on flux x cell area, named for v2. TOTALS include the aviation climb/descent and cruise sectors (TNR_Aviation_CDS/CRS), which a surface-only frame puts at the surface. NOx is NO2-equivalent mass (Crippa et al. 2023, ESSD 15, 2667). Every file's global integral on the authalic sphere (R = 6371007.2 m) reproduces its fluxes:global_total attribute (CO 450.16, NOx 109.60, NH3 57.32, NMVOC 138.12, PM2.5 37.03, PM10 57.61 Mt). BC and OC go to the hydrophobic rows only, as WRF's emiss_opt=6 block does (chem/emissions_driver.F:1604-1607)."
